            "path": "apps/web/components/map/NaverMapView.tsx",
            "line": 2086,
            "body": "**<sub><sub>![P2 Badge](https://img.shields.io/badge/P2-yellow?style=flat)</sub></sub>  Resolve retained marker tiers from the publication index**\n\nWhen a published restaurant is retained outside the current query result, these values come directly from the selected/searched object rather than the publication lookup. For example, home-history restoration recreates `searchedRestaurant` from a compact snapshot that omits `popularity_tier`; if that restaurant is outside the restored bounds or filters, `buildRestaurantsForSwipe` renders that object and `getNaverIndividualMarkerVisual` normalizes it to `standard`, even though the detail panel resolves the same ID to `fire` or `rainbow`. Project retained selected/search objects through the published lookup before building both the signature and marker visual so restored or other raw entry paths remain consistent.\n\nUseful? React with 👍 / 👎.\n\n<!-- codex-code-review-finding:v1 -->"
          }
        ]
      }
